n":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":11,"created_at":"2026-06-21T10:11:10Z","updated_at":"2026-06-23T08:31:47Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120513","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120513","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120513.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120513.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\nLaunching a game on Linux Wayland is almost impossible in non-tab mode now because of someone who enabled window embedding on Wayland, editor almost fully freezes after launch.\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nAfter some weir actions I figured out that when you launch in separate window editor starts to freeze because treats Godot's window and game window as one (this works perfectly on DMs with embedding support). Cause of this is auto using XWayland on launch, this causes Godot to think this is X11 env, making whole `platform/linuxbsd/wayland/display_server_wayland.cpp` dead/useless code.\r\n\r\n#### So this PR adds\r\n\r\n- Runtime Wayland detection (dlopen/dlsym)\r\n- Hide unsupported settings (expand_to_title and game_embed_mode)\r\n- Signal connection fix (play_pressed/stop_pressed)\r\n- XWayland warning\r\n\r\nFixes #119243 \r\nFixes #102580 ","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120513/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120513/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}